# Day 2 — The LLM Landscape

## What I learned

- Training helps a model learn patterns from data by adjusting its parameters.
- Pre-training teaches a language model general patterns from a large training corpus.
- A base model can undergo fine-tuning and other post-training processes to improve its behavior.
- During text generation, an LLM predicts tokens based on the context it receives.
- An LLM does not necessarily search its original training data every time it answers a question.
- An LLM application is software that uses a language model to provide a particular experience or solve a problem.
- Evaluation and monitoring help developers assess and improve AI systems.

## What confused me

- I initially thought an LLM always searches a data storage system before answering.
- I confused an LLM with an LLM application.
- I want to understand more about how the different layers of an LLM work together.

## My takeaway

I learned more about training, pre-training, fine-tuning, and how language models become useful assistants. What fascinated me most was the architecture of an LLM and how its different layers process information to generate text.
